// Slide 6: Ingestion Workflow
#slide(title: "Ingestion: Generation & Storage")[
  *Prefect Flow:* `refill_bucket_flow`
  
  #cols(columns: (1fr, 1fr), gutter: 2em)[
    #rect(fill: rgb("#e6fffa"), inset: 10pt, radius: 5pt, width: 100%)[
      *1. Generator (`seed_script.py`)*
      - `contents.csv` (Catalog)
      - `users.csv` (User Base)
      - `viewing_logs.json` (High Vol.)
      - `mentions.json` (Unstructured)
    ]
  ][
    #rect(fill: rgb("#e6f7ff"), inset: 10pt, radius: 5pt, width: 100%)[
      *2. Data Lake (GCS)*
      - Bucket: `raw_data/ingested-data`
      - *Partitioning:* By Date/Run
      - *Safety:* Idempotent execution
    ]
  ]

  #v(1em)
  *Key Technical Choice:* 
  Simulating a live production environment rather than static file uploads.
]

// Slide 7: Transformation Layer
#slide(title: "Transformation Strategy (dbt)")[
  *The "Medallion" Architecture in BigQuery*

  #grid(
    columns: (1fr, auto, 1fr, auto, 1fr),
    gutter: 0.5em,
    align: horizon,
    
    // Bronze
    rect(fill: rgb("#cd7f32"), inset: 10pt, radius: 5pt, width: 100%)[
      #align(center)[*Bronze* \ (Raw)]
      #text(size: 0.6em)[External Tables (No Load Cost)]
    ],
    $->$,
    // Silver
    rect(fill: rgb("#c0c0c0"), inset: 10pt, radius: 5pt, width: 100%)[
      #align(center)[*Silver* \ (Staging/Int)]
      #text(size: 0.6em)[Cleaning & Deduplication]
    ],
    $->$,
    // Gold
    rect(fill: rgb("#ffd700"), inset: 10pt, radius: 5pt, width: 100%)[
      #align(center)[*Gold* \ (Marts)]
      #text(size: 0.6em)[Star Schema (Facts/Dims)]
    ]
  )

  #v(1em)
  
  #cols(columns: (1fr, 1fr), gutter: 1em)[
    *Layer Details*
    - *Staging:* 1:1 Views, Renaming.
    - *Intermediate:* Complex joins (e.g., `int__viewing_enriched`).
    - *Marts:* Final Business Logic.
  ][
    *Why External Tables?*
    We query GCS directly using `create_external_sources`. 
    - No data duplication.
    - Lower storage costs.
  ]
]
